    "scenesThatPass": [
      "MOTHER BARBARA: Pray girls. Pray for the Magdalen.\nANUNCIATA: Reverend Mother, please - we must get a doctor. The baby is the wrong way round, it’s breech.\nMOTHER BARBARA: It’s in God’s hands now.",
      "PHILOMENA: We were allowed to see our children for an hour a day, that was all.\nMOTHER BARBARA: Walk don’t run!",
      "PHILOMENA: As soon as I saw their lovely clothes, and Mother Barbara so happy and smiling, I knew all hope was gone.\nYOUNG SISTER HILDEGARDE: Come away from there!\nYOUNG SISTER HILDEGARDE: What are you doing out here?\nYOUNG PHILOMENA: I... I had a stomach ache, Sister Hidegarde. It’s my time of the month.",
      "PHILOMENA: Some of them were nice.\nJANE: It was a breech birth and they wouldn’t even give her painkillers.",
      "JANE: I’m taking mum to Ireland next week for a few days - why don’t you come along with us and you can visit Roscrea with her?\nPHILOMENA: Oh yes there’s plenty of room - it’s a Vauxhall Cavalier."
    ]
  },
